Subject: X11 starts only when an X11 program needs it

KWin starts Xwayland the first time a program connects to the display.
Three parts of the session connected at every sign-in, so Xwayland, and the
X11 helpers that come with it, were always in memory (about 30 MB):

  * ksmserver forced the xcb platform. On Wayland it now runs on the
    minimal platform (offscreen opens an X display of its own); it shows
    no window. The legacy session save (WM_COMMAND of X11 programs
    without session management) is X11 only and is skipped on Wayland.
  * the appmenu kded module opened an X connection when it loaded, used
    only when an X11 window registers a menu. It connects then.
  * kcminit wrote the X resources (xrdb) and the root cursor. On Wayland
    this waits for Xwayland: Raye's Xwayland-session.d hook runs kcminit
    for the fonts and style modules when it starts.

Reason: each of these connects to the display from compiled code at
sign-in; no setting, environment variable or script can keep them off X11
without also breaking them, as tried on 2026-11-19 (hiding DISPLAY from
kcminit and masking ksmserver still left kded's appmenu starting Xwayland).

